          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Keep two things on the garage shelf: a pack of oil-only pads such as PIG MAT403 or Brady BPO100, and a bag of granules, diatomaceous earth from EP Minerals if you want light and thirsty, Oil-Dri clay if you want cheap. Add PIG Lite-Dri if your spills tend to happen on a wet driveway, a couple of socks for containment, and a Drymate mat under any car that drips.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Absorb first, grind granules in, give them time, and only then wash. Dispose of the used material the way your town asks. Done within the hour, most spills never become stains, and that is cheaper than any stain remover on the market.
